From 3b8644425c70782f92106ada889bfd77d9bb15ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:28:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 247/270] tegra_dc: mirror the panel on an HDMI screen

While the hot plug line (GPIO N7 on the AC100) shows a screen, power
the HDMI block (TPS6586x LDO7 and LDO8), read the screen's EDID over
the DDC bus (I2C2), set PLL_D to twice the pixel clock and start
display controller B and the HDMI serializer. Display controller B
scans out the panel's frame buffer, scaled to the screen's preferred
mode without changing its proportions, or to 1280x720 without a
usable EDID mode. HDMI sinks get an AVI infoframe, DVI sinks plain
TMDS. Unplugging stops everything again.

'hdmi false' in the tegra_dc driver settings keeps the HDMI block off.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
